WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.057 --> 00:00:03.834
-Half of all adults in the US
have now received

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:06.634
at least one shot
of the COVID-19 vaccine,

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:09.167
and as of today,
all adults are eligible,

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:11.100
and as a result,
even Republicans are admitting

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.200
they're having a hard time
criticizing President Biden.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.267
For more on this,
it's time for A Closer Look.

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:20.033
♪♪

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:22.968
As horrific and nightmarish
as the pandemic has been --

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:24.767
and it is by no means over,

00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:26.300
especially throughout
the rest of the world --

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.534
we are now hitting some
genuinely exciting milestones.

00:00:29.534 --> 00:00:33.100
-The race to vaccinate hitting
two major milestones today.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.868
The CDC reports that
50% of all adults

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:38.000
have received at least
one vaccine dose,

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.367
and 25% of all Americans
are now fully vaccinated.

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:44.167
-Starting today, every adult
across the nation

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:45.968
is eligible
to get a COVID shot.

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:02.801
-When I think back
to the lowest points

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:04.734
of this hellish year,
there were times when it was

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:06.901
impossible to imagine
the progress we're seeing now.

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:09.667
There were times when I honestly
thought there was a chance

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:11.300
I'd be locked in
the captain's quarters

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.868
talking to a painting
for the rest of my life,

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:15.801
urinating into jars,
growing a long, scraggly beard,

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:18.667
and rolling my eyes
at dumb, maritime-themed puns.

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:22.501
Thankfully, thankfully,
that ship has sailed. I'm sorry.

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:24.400
Half of adults have now
gotten at least one shot

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.100
and all adults
in the US are eligible.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.100
It's a dramatic achievement
worthy of celebration,

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.000
especially considering where
we were just a few months ago.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.868
Before the previous president
left office,

00:01:32.868 --> 00:01:34.767
the vaccine rollout
was in chaos.

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:37.167
His administration had passed
on the opportunity

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:38.334
to buy more vaccine,

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:40.133
and they'd made
all kinds of wild

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.634
and obviously insane promises,

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.601
like the time
Trump's Chief of Staff

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:45.534
said they'd have
100 million doses

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:49.267
by October and enough vaccine
for every American by January.

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:52.501
-We use all of our regulatory
tools to bring vaccine available

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:55.567
for the entire American
population by January.

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:58.601
-You know, in terms of
the number of vials,

00:01:58.601 --> 00:02:00.901
what we're shooting for
is to try to make sure

00:02:00.901 --> 00:02:04.133
that we have 100 million doses
in that first tranche,

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:06.767
and so those --
that 100 million doses

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:11.100
certainly is the benchmark
that we've set.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.868
From there, there would be
a second tranche

00:02:12.868 --> 00:02:17.501
that would get us up to
the 300 million plus doses.

00:02:17.501 --> 00:02:21.934
That timeline for
the 300 million is set

00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:26.167
as a January timeline, in terms
of what we're looking at.

00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:27.267
-He's so cagey.

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:28.901
He's talking
about vaccine distribution

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:31.467
like he's telling a loan shark
when he can expect his money.

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:32.834
[ Nervously ] Yeah, I'm going to
get you your money.

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:34.601
I got a job now
and I stopped gambling.

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:36.467
No more betting
on the ponies for me.

00:02:36.467 --> 00:02:37.567
No, siree.

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:39.033
When can I have it buy? Uhh...

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:41.400
Let's see, the Kentucky Derby
is the first Saturday in May,

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.334
so the first Sunday in May?

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:46.734
[ Normally ] And yes, when Biden
took office and only promised

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:49.067
100 hundred million shots
in the first 100 days,

00:02:49.067 --> 00:02:50.601
that was clearly
a lowball number,

00:02:50.601 --> 00:02:54.601
but it made sense to set lower
expectations after the last guys

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:58.234
overpromised on everything every
time they opened their mouths.

00:02:58.234 --> 00:02:59.767
Not only do we think
we will have

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:01.701
300 hundred million vaccines
by January,

00:03:01.701 --> 00:03:03.434
but we are now closer
than ever to getting

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:06.133
every American
the nootropic pill, NZT-48,

00:03:06.133 --> 00:03:07.801
also known as
the "Limitless" pill,

00:03:07.801 --> 00:03:09.234
taken by Bradley Cooper
in the film "Limitless".

00:03:09.234 --> 00:03:11.601
And as a reminder, this is
a pill that will allow us

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:13.801
to use our whole brain
with no side effects.

00:03:13.801 --> 00:03:16.200
At least I think
that's the case, as I will admit

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:19.734
I only watched
the first tranche of that movie.

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:22.067
Anyway, that obviously
all turned out to be [bleep].

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:24.167
The Trump administration
had no interest

00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:26.968
in actually overseeing
an effective vaccine rollout,

00:03:26.968 --> 00:03:28.601
so they just passed it off
to the states

00:03:28.601 --> 00:03:30.567
and it was, initially,
a disaster.

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:32.968
Biden, meanwhile, secured deals
to buy more vaccine,

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:36.100
brokered deals between rivals
to produce more vaccine,

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:38.901
and quickly ramped up
a plan to use FEMA

00:03:38.901 --> 00:03:41.501
to set up federally-run
mass vaccination sites

00:03:41.501 --> 00:03:44.567
across the country, which for
some reason, Trump failed to do.

00:03:44.567 --> 00:03:47.334
Maybe because he didn't know
what FEMA stood for

00:03:47.334 --> 00:03:48.968
and was too embarrassed to ask.

00:03:48.968 --> 00:03:51.400
Sir, we should coordinate
between HHS and FEMA.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:52.267
[ Imitating Trump ]
Right, right, right.

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:54.634
The Federal...Elegant...

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.834
Modeling Agency, is that right?

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:59.100
So the models, they would
administer the vaccines --

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:00.367
and only 10s, right?

00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:03.367
Nobody's going to roll up
their sleeve for a 7.

00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:05.000
I could tell you that.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.501
[ Normally ] But as encouraging
as the vaccine rollout has been

00:04:07.501 --> 00:04:10.234
here in the US, it's been
much less encouraging throughout

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:12.100
the rest of the world,
thanks in large part

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.567
to vaccine hoarding
by wealthy countries.

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:17.434
Global COVID cases
just hit a new weekly record,

00:04:17.434 --> 00:04:19.734
making this the worst week
worldwide

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:21.367
since the start
of the pandemic.

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:24.400
And that's why we need a more
just and equitable distribution

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:25.834
of vaccines
to developing nations.

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:27.667
So far, high-income countries

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:30.968
already own more than half of
all global doses purchased,

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:33.767
and it's estimated that there
will not be enough vaccine doses

00:04:33.767 --> 00:04:34.968
to cover the world's population

00:04:34.968 --> 00:04:36.267
until at least 2023.

00:04:36.267 --> 00:04:38.434
Meanwhile, the US could have
300 hundred million

00:04:38.434 --> 00:04:40.868
extra vaccine doses
by the end of July.

00:04:40.868 --> 00:04:43.033
Let's send those extra vaccines
to countries that need them.

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:44.667
We certainly don't need them
here.

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:46.667
As a country, we don't do well
with excess.

00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:47.968
We'll start having raves

00:04:47.968 --> 00:04:49.934
where Wall Street bros
and social media influencers

00:04:49.934 --> 00:04:52.267
pass vials of Pfizer
in bathrooms

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:54.434
while dancing poorly
to club music.

00:04:54.434 --> 00:04:56.734
♪ Shots, shots, shots, shots,
shots, shots ♪

00:04:58.901 --> 00:05:00.934
Hey man. [ Laughs ]

00:05:00.934 --> 00:05:03.100
Hey man, you want a hit of
this uncut Pfizer?

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:04.400
You'll have a sore arm for
a few days,

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:08.367
but then you'll be
[stammers] sky high.

00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:10.868
I was thrown by the shots.
It was in the script,

00:05:10.868 --> 00:05:12.534
but I still forgot
what it would sound like.

00:05:12.534 --> 00:05:15.200
♪ Shots, shots, shots, shots,
shots, shots ♪

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.567
Now it's coming back.

00:05:16.567 --> 00:05:18.901
Ah. It's like sense memory,
you know?

00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:20.400
I was like,
"What is that jarring sound?"

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:21.734
And then I'm like, "Oh, right."

00:05:21.734 --> 00:05:23.868
Da club.

00:05:23.868 --> 00:05:27.701
Also, it's in our own interest
to share our vaccines as well.

00:05:27.701 --> 00:05:30.901
If we don't slow down the spread
of the virus around the world,

00:05:30.901 --> 00:05:32.334
then more variants will emerge,

00:05:32.334 --> 00:05:34.133
and we can't just stop them
from coming here

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:36.801
by increasing the US
in a protective bubble like

00:05:36.801 --> 00:05:40.067
we're in some Stephen King novel
or The Simpsons movie.

00:05:40.067 --> 00:05:42.834
Almost identical plots.
Crazy, but it's true.

00:05:42.834 --> 00:05:44.634
Nonetheless, there's hope
on the vaccine front.

00:05:44.634 --> 00:05:47.501
So much so that Biden's approval
numbers in a recent poll

00:05:47.501 --> 00:05:48.801
are as high as 59%,

00:05:48.801 --> 00:05:51.133
with only 39% saying
they disapprove.

00:05:51.133 --> 00:05:53.801
And now, as a result
of Biden's early popularity,

00:05:53.801 --> 00:05:55.501
a weird thing is happening,

00:05:55.501 --> 00:05:57.501
which is Republicans
are basically admitting

00:05:57.501 --> 00:05:59.167
they don't know
how to criticize it.

00:05:59.167 --> 00:06:01.701
After four years of a cruel,
unpopular, crazy person

00:06:01.701 --> 00:06:02.934
who never won
the popular vote

00:06:02.934 --> 00:06:04.767
and never cracked
50% job approval

00:06:04.767 --> 00:06:07.467
or a 50-degree angle
on his spine,

00:06:07.467 --> 00:06:10.200
Republicans can't quite figure
out how to attack a president

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.501
who is well-liked
and his policies are popular.

00:06:12.501 --> 00:06:14.200
John Thune,
the #2 Senate Republican,

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:16.634
said, "I don't think
sometimes our messaging

00:06:16.634 --> 00:06:19.000
is as sharp as it should be,
because a lot of the things

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.033
they're doing are things
that are popular --

00:06:21.033 --> 00:06:23.200
when you're spending money,
you're popular."

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.033
He added of Biden,
"His tone is moderate

00:06:25.033 --> 00:06:26.234
and he's an affable person,

00:06:26.234 --> 00:06:27.601
he's a likable individual,

00:06:27.601 --> 00:06:29.901
and a lot of us know him,
have relationships with him,

00:06:29.901 --> 00:06:31.801
and it's probably harder
to attack someone

00:06:31.801 --> 00:06:33.667
who is relatable
and likable."

00:06:33.667 --> 00:06:36.234
Relatable, likable,
and doing popular things --

00:06:36.234 --> 00:06:37.734
what is he,
some kind of sorcerer?

00:06:37.734 --> 00:06:39.200
How does he do it?

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.334
They're watching Biden like
a bunch of prehistoric apes

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:43.267
watching man make
the first stone tools.

00:06:43.267 --> 00:06:45.501
"Well, this isn't going to be
fair now."

00:06:45.501 --> 00:06:46.901
Remember,
Republicans have only won

00:06:46.901 --> 00:06:49.501
the presidential popular vote
once in the last 32 years.

00:06:49.501 --> 00:06:52.734
They're used to being unpopular
and just having the edge

00:06:52.734 --> 00:06:54.400
because of our unfair
electoral system.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:56.767
They're genuinely befuddled
by a president

00:06:56.767 --> 00:06:59.200
who's likable,
doing popular stuff,

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:00.834
even if it's obvious
to the rest of us.

00:07:00.834 --> 00:07:02.667
Republicans are so desperate
to criticize Biden,

00:07:02.667 --> 00:07:04.934
their only move
is to call him a puppet.

00:07:04.934 --> 00:07:07.467
Yesterday, Fox News interviewed
GOP Congressman Devin Nunes,

00:07:07.467 --> 00:07:09.033
who, speaking of puppets,
looks like his eyes

00:07:09.033 --> 00:07:12.167
were hastily sewn onto his face.
Remember that guy?

00:07:12.167 --> 00:07:14.667
He always looks like
the claw machine dropped his

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:16.467
Beanie Baby at the last second.

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:19.801
Nunes suggested that
there was actually

00:07:19.801 --> 00:07:21.868
some secret group
of puppet masters

00:07:21.868 --> 00:07:23.367
pulling the strings
behind Biden.

00:07:23.367 --> 00:07:26.300
-The question is, is we don't
see a lot of Biden every day.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:27.734
I don't know, you know --
and of course,

00:07:27.734 --> 00:07:29.033
nobody's really calling him out

00:07:29.033 --> 00:07:30.367
on, you know,
what is his schedule?

00:07:30.367 --> 00:07:31.934
What is he actually doing?

00:07:31.934 --> 00:07:33.133
I think a lot of us wonder.

00:07:33.133 --> 00:07:35.033
And we didn't even see him
in the campaign.

00:07:35.033 --> 00:07:37.968
So, you know, somebody clearly
is behind the scenes

00:07:37.968 --> 00:07:40.701
controlling the -- building
these narratives out,

00:07:40.701 --> 00:07:44.100
and they they put their people
out, and their mouthpieces.

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:46.133
-It's true. But you never
heard Trump speak

00:07:46.133 --> 00:07:47.567
or read one of his tweets
and thought,

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:49.567
"Who's making him say that?"

00:07:49.567 --> 00:07:50.934
But come on,
Biden was literally

00:07:50.934 --> 00:07:52.601
just in the Rose Garden
for press conference

00:07:52.601 --> 00:07:54.334
with the Prime Minister
of Japan on Friday.

00:07:54.334 --> 00:07:56.100
I know you guys
only go on "Fox News",

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:58.000
but do you also
only watch "Fox News"?

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.334
I'm guessing anytime
Biden gives a speech,

00:08:00.334 --> 00:08:03.367
Fox throws to some emergency
standby episode

00:08:03.367 --> 00:08:07.033
of Jeanine Pirro's short-lived
wine-tasting show, Jeanine
Pinot.

00:08:07.033 --> 00:08:08.767
[ Imitating Pirro ] Now, the
first thing we always do

00:08:08.767 --> 00:08:10.133
is inhale the bouquet.

00:08:10.133 --> 00:08:13.334
[ Sniffs ]
Smells like wine to me!

00:08:13.334 --> 00:08:14.934
Which means we're on to
step two --

00:08:14.934 --> 00:08:18.000
downing it in one big-ass gulp.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:23.701
And to answer your question,
no, you cannot have my keys.

00:08:23.701 --> 00:08:25.367
[ Normally ] Also, you really
have questions about what

00:08:25.367 --> 00:08:26.567
Joe Biden does all day?

00:08:26.567 --> 00:08:27.667
Say what you want about the guy,

00:08:27.667 --> 00:08:29.467
but he has that energy
of a grandpa

00:08:29.467 --> 00:08:31.000
who insists on getting up
at 4:00 AM

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:32.367
to go for
his daily power walk

00:08:32.367 --> 00:08:33.501
on the side
of the highway.

00:08:33.501 --> 00:08:34.968
"Grandpa, just stay
in the cul de sac."

00:08:34.968 --> 00:08:37.801
[ Loudly ] I like to dodge the
cars. It keeps me in shape.

00:08:37.801 --> 00:08:40.000
Give me my three-pounders!

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:41.501
[ Normally ] Trump, meanwhile,
spent so little time

00:08:41.501 --> 00:08:43.968
in the Oval Office, they could
have rented it out on Airbnb --

00:08:43.968 --> 00:08:46.934
which, by the way, would have
been a great early 2000s comedy

00:08:46.934 --> 00:08:48.834
starring Owen Wilson
and Vince Vaughn.

00:08:48.834 --> 00:08:50.400
[ Imitating Wilson ]
Oh jeez, that's a bust

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:52.634
of Abraham Lincoln?
I thought that was an ashtray.

00:08:52.634 --> 00:08:53.701
[ Imitating Vaughn ]
Buddy, buddy, buddy.

00:08:53.701 --> 00:08:54.968
We got to get out
of here, buddy.

00:08:54.968 --> 00:08:56.334
I just hooked up
with the Secretary of State

00:08:56.334 --> 00:08:58.467
and now she won't
leave me alone.

00:08:58.467 --> 00:09:00.834
We got to go, buddy.

00:09:00.834 --> 00:09:02.501
[ Normally ] Similarly,
Texas Senator John Cornyn

00:09:02.501 --> 00:09:05.601
suggested last week that Biden
was perhaps being controlled

00:09:05.601 --> 00:09:07.100
by a secret group
of leftists

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.934
when he quoted
a political article

00:09:08.934 --> 00:09:11.467
about Biden's communications
strategy and added this --

00:09:11.467 --> 00:09:13.567
"Invites the question:
is he really in charge?"

00:09:13.567 --> 00:09:15.234
On Sunday, Cornyn was asked

00:09:15.234 --> 00:09:17.234
about that tweet
and blamed Twitter.

00:09:17.234 --> 00:09:19.467
-My question, I guess,
is Senator Cornyn,

00:09:19.467 --> 00:09:23.200
is that helpful to be
sending out a tweet questioning

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:26.734
the -- President Biden's
mental faculties?

00:09:26.734 --> 00:09:28.234
-Well, Chris, thank you
for the question,

00:09:28.234 --> 00:09:30.334
because I think there's been
a lot of confusion

00:09:30.334 --> 00:09:32.100
in the Twitterverse about that.

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:35.167
That actually was a quote
from a "Politico" story

00:09:35.167 --> 00:09:37.501
that I pasted into a tweet,

00:09:37.501 --> 00:09:39.567
and then I simply
asked a question.

00:09:39.567 --> 00:09:41.100
-Man, I never want to hear
a man your age

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:42.167
say the word "Twitterverse."

00:09:42.167 --> 00:09:43.734
It's like watching
your dad twerk.

00:09:43.734 --> 00:09:46.200
"Dad, knock it off. You're
getting loose change
everywhere."

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:48.434
That's how at a loss these guys
are to criticize Biden.

00:09:48.434 --> 00:09:49.567
And by the way,
that's not to say

00:09:49.567 --> 00:09:50.934
there aren't things to
criticize.

00:09:50.934 --> 00:09:52.434
There absolutely are.
For example, last week

00:09:52.434 --> 00:09:54.868
Biden announced and quickly
walked back his decision

00:09:54.868 --> 00:09:57.501
to break a campaign pledge
and keep in place

00:09:57.501 --> 00:10:00.234
the historically low cap
on refugee admissions

00:10:00.234 --> 00:10:02.534
set by the Trump administration
rather than lift it

00:10:02.534 --> 00:10:03.868
as he promised
during the election.

00:10:03.868 --> 00:10:05.400
The Biden administration
tried to reverse

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:07.501
that announcement
after progressives

00:10:07.501 --> 00:10:10.601
and refugee advocates
were rightfully outraged.

00:10:10.601 --> 00:10:13.834
Today, NBC News has learned
the Biden administration

00:10:13.834 --> 00:10:16.200
intends to keep the cap
for refugee admissions

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:19.667
at 15,000 -- this according to a
senior administration official.

00:10:19.667 --> 00:10:22.801
It is a historically low level
set by the previous

00:10:22.801 --> 00:10:23.934
Trump administration.

00:10:23.934 --> 00:10:25.767
-The Biden administration is now
reversing course

00:10:25.767 --> 00:10:28.167
on its announcement that it
would keep the refugee cap

00:10:28.167 --> 00:10:30.968
of 15,000 set
by the Trump administration,

00:10:30.968 --> 00:10:34.601
after facing fierce backlash
for some progressive Democrats.

00:10:34.601 --> 00:10:37.334
-On Twitter, Representative
Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez

00:10:37.334 --> 00:10:39.334
condemned the decision,
saying, quote,

00:10:39.334 --> 00:10:41.667
"It's completely
and utterly unacceptable.

00:10:41.667 --> 00:10:43.300
Biden promised
to welcome immigrants

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:45.968
and people voted for him
based on that promise.

00:10:45.968 --> 00:10:48.067
Upholding the xenophobic
and racist policies

00:10:48.067 --> 00:10:49.434
of the Trump administration,

00:10:49.434 --> 00:10:52.767
including the historically
low + plummeted refugee cap

00:10:52.767 --> 00:10:55.467
is flat out wrong.
Keep your promise."

00:10:55.467 --> 00:10:57.801
-Pramila Jayapal,
a House member who's the leader

00:10:57.801 --> 00:10:59.634
of the Progressive Caucus,
saying, quote,

00:10:59.634 --> 00:11:01.934
"It is simply unacceptable
and unconscionable

00:11:01.934 --> 00:11:04.801
that the Biden administration
is not immediately repealing

00:11:04.801 --> 00:11:07.067
Donald Trump's harmful,
xenophobic, and racist

00:11:07.067 --> 00:11:10.467
refugee cap that cruelly
restricts refugee admissions

00:11:10.467 --> 00:11:12.534
to a historically low level."

00:11:12.534 --> 00:11:15.467
-Sources say that
President Biden has resisted

00:11:15.467 --> 00:11:19.234
raising the Trump-era cap
on refugees

00:11:19.234 --> 00:11:21.901
because of bad political optics.

00:11:21.901 --> 00:11:23.567
-Oh, so you were worried
about optics?

00:11:23.567 --> 00:11:25.334
What's worse
in terms of optics?

00:11:25.334 --> 00:11:27.300
Breaking a campaign promise
to lift a cruel

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:30.300
and historically low refugee cap
set by racist predecessor,

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:35.067
or tripping upwards
on the stairs three times?

00:11:35.067 --> 00:11:38.033
And again, the best part of
the three-trip walk up --

00:11:38.033 --> 00:11:40.801
the salute
at the end to save it.

00:11:40.801 --> 00:11:42.033
Look, we all trip, it's fine.

00:11:42.033 --> 00:11:43.634
It's like when you eat [bleep]
an icy sidewalk

00:11:43.634 --> 00:11:45.200
then give everyone a thumbs up.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:47.767
As for the optics, Republicans
are never, ever going to

00:11:47.767 --> 00:11:49.501
give you credit for anything,
so stop chasing it.

00:11:49.501 --> 00:11:51.634
Republicans are
like an emotionally distant dad,

00:11:51.634 --> 00:11:53.400
from the '50s, who sends you
to boarding school

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.934
where you could get
straight "A"s,

00:11:54.934 --> 00:11:56.534
But if you're 5 minutes late
for dinner,

00:11:56.534 --> 00:11:58.000
he'll say something cutting
without looking up

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:01.567
from his paper like "You
call yourself an Exeter man?"

00:12:01.567 --> 00:12:03.167
Voters were craving
competent governments

00:12:03.167 --> 00:12:05.901
after four years
of cruelty, racism, and neglect,

00:12:05.901 --> 00:12:07.868
and now they're rewarding Biden
for it in the polls.

00:12:07.868 --> 00:12:09.934
The left absolutely
must keep pushing him on issues

00:12:09.934 --> 00:12:12.701
like refugee admissions
and global vaccine distribution,

00:12:12.701 --> 00:12:14.934
because Biden is clearly
willing to react

00:12:14.934 --> 00:12:16.334
to pressure from progressives.

00:12:16.334 --> 00:12:18.934
As for Republicans,
all they seem capable of doing

00:12:18.934 --> 00:12:20.734
is spending their time
whining in...

00:12:20.734 --> 00:12:22.000
-The Twitterverse.

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:23.400
This has been A Closer Look.

